\caption{Per-layer $R^2$ action-probe profiles for three architectures, each comparing trained (solid) and untrained (dashed) checkpoints.
All VLM-to-VLA trained cells exhibit pronounced peak-to-exit collapse ($\Delta R^2 = 0.16$--$0.36$), while untrained VLM baselines show near-flat profiles ($\Delta R^2 \leq 0.09$).
OpenVLA (VLA-to-VLA) shows substantially smaller collapse ($\Delta R^2 = 0.03$--$0.12$); the OXE-pretrained baseline has already undergone exit-layer reorganization.}

